# Line endings: LF, the Linux convention, in the repository and in every checkout,
# whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The fixture bundle under reskit/data/test_cache is catalogued data: every file must
# check out byte-for-byte as committed, or its SHA-256 no longer matches the ETHOS.Data
# catalogue and `reskit-data bundle verify` fails (as it did on the Windows runners, where
# core.autocrlf=true rewrote the LF text fixtures). No conversion in either direction.
reskit/data/test_cache/** -text
